1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:07,180
A new motion picture colour negative stock, Kodak's VERITA 200D, launched in April 2026.

2
00:00:07,530 --> 00:00:13,590
For film labs, every new stock is another argument for ECN-2 processing capacity.

3
00:00:14,090 --> 00:00:19,600
It is a 200-speed, daylight-balanced stock built for a classic cinema look.

4
00:00:19,950 --> 00:00:28,630
It launched in three formats at once, 65, 35 and 16 millimetre, and joins the VISION3 family rather than replacing it.

5
00:00:29,130 --> 00:00:33,420
Like VISION3, it runs through ECN-2 chemistry, not C-41.

6
00:00:33,770 --> 00:00:40,590
A still-photography lab running C-41 cannot process it without dedicated ECN-2 equipment.

7
00:00:41,090 --> 00:00:46,440
A three-format launch and a widening stock catalogue point to processing volume that is growing.

8
00:00:46,790 --> 00:00:51,240
That is the case for owning ECN-2 capacity rather than outsourcing indefinitely.

9
00:00:51,740 --> 00:01:03,760
Micrographics Data makes the ECN-PRO and ECN-PRO3 processors, built around 16 and 35 millimetre ECN-2 work and configured to your volume and stock mix.

10
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:06,620
Get your lab ready for the next stock.

11
00:01:06,970 --> 00:01:09,770
Request a quote at micrographicsdata.com.
